n when a query depends on duplicate addresses, invalid/unreadable files, out-of-repo sources, escaping symlinks, dynamic sources, splat/index-dependent traversals, computed values, or provider-defined attributes.'; and 'Exceeding any bound yields one abstention'","norm_id":"n52cc512d2b0c4c8b","priority":0.4467,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A query hits a computed attribute value — the tool must emit abstain but no enum reason clearly fits, so implementers pick divergently (other vs ambiguous), breaking the exact-reason oracle in AC 'computed/provider/dynamic/ambiguous cases return a closed abstention'","A closure exceeds 5000 files — implementers disagree whether that is 'other' or a new reason, and the AC oracle 'exact outcome/reason' cannot be met"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"In the Structural index / Operations sections, give the trigger→abstain_reason table, e.g. duplicate addresses→ambiguous, invalid/unreadable→parse_error, out-of-repo/escaping-symlink→private_or_internal_suspected (or other), computed/provider/dynamic/splat-index→other, and 64-module/5000-file/32-MiB breach→other; if none fit computed/limits, note the required enum extension in grounding.schema.json.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.6667,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["4 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"Confirm and state that python-hcl2 line locations require enabling __start_line__/__end_line__ metadata and yield line-level (not column/byte-span) granularity, and reconcile that with the plan's 'parser locations' and receipt 'span' claims.","cohort":["T1"],"criteria":["T1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.568,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan text: 'Use parser locations for HCL. For Terraform JSON, return an exact line only for an unambiguous key occurrence; otherwise return file-level location.'","Plan text (receipts): 'return type, safe classification such as wildcard/empty, digest, and span.'","Retrieved python-hcl2 getting-started docs list 'Add __start_line__ / __end_line__ metadata' as a configurable option (not default), and DeepWiki notes metadata is line-number annotation on dictionaries used for reconstruction.","python-hcl2 returns a Python dict (per PyPI/GitHub description: 'A parser for HCL2 ... returns a python dictionary'), which yields line-level, not column/byte-span, positions."],"finding":"The plan relies on python-hcl2 emitting source locations ('Use parser locations for HCL', 'return an exact line', receipts include a 'span'), but does not resolve that python-hcl2 exposes line data only via opt-in __start_line__/__end_line__ metadata on a flattened dict — i.e. line granularity, not column/byte spans — leaving a load-bearing capability assertion unverified.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fa1ab242ee8636905","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope > Structural index ('Use parser locations for HCL. For Terraform JSON, return an exact line...') and Operations and receipts ('...digest, and span.')","norm_id":"ncf0a0efd746ed799","priority":0.132,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A T10 finding needs a precise span for a resource attribute but python-hcl2 only yields the block's start/end line.","Line metadata is not enabled in the worker call, so evidence carries no location at all and every HCL lookup silently degrades to file-level."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add a one-line capability note: python-hcl2 must be invoked with __start_line__/__end_line__ metadata enabled and provides line-level positions only; define 'span' in receipts as a start/end line range (with file-level fallback) rather than a byte/column span.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius"